A stateful property compares generated commands with real behavior. Deterministic initial state makes failures reproducible and shrinkable. Check the model by injecting a [defect](/lore/effect-basics).

> Both function calls must be deterministic.

Source: [Q17](/lore/durability-bibliography#q17); [B11](/lore/durability-bibliography#b11-property-based-testing), [B4](/lore/durability-bibliography#b4-release-it), [B15](/lore/durability-bibliography#b15-software-engineering-at-google).

## Failure it prevents

A vacuous or happy-path suite misses corruption across retries, cancellation, and restart.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

`Arbitrary.checkEffect` and @[effect](/lore/effect-basics)/vitest run properties. `TestClock` and `Deferred` control `Effect` time and coordination. Author the command model; test persistent backends separately.

Source: `packages/effect/src/Arbitrary.ts`, `packages/effect/src/testing/TestClock.ts`, `packages/effect/src/Deferred.ts`.

## How to check

Plant a known transition bug. Require the property to fail and yield a replayable, valid counterexample. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Checkpoints follow the promised commit](/lore/checkpoints-follow-commits), [Circuit breakers have state](/lore/circuit-breakers-have-state).

Connect this to [property-based testing](/lore/property-based-testing) and [model-based testing](/lore/model-based-testing).

